        "original_id": "f28e7014-cff2-5d51-af98-5c91e175bd80",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jacques Demy, Paul Sloane, Stepin Fetchit, Cary Grant, Joan Bennett, Randolph Scott, Walter Brennan\n- Roles: film directors, writers\n- Works: The Umbrellas of Cherbourg, The Young Girls of Rochefort, Hearts in Dixie, The Woman Accused, The Texans\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Sloane was born on April 19, 1893, and died on November 15, 1963.\n- Paul Sloane was a writer and film director who directed 26 films from 1925 to 1952 and wrote or co-wrote 35 films.\n- Paul Sloane directed Hearts in Dixie in 1929, and the film featured Stepin Fetchit.\n- Paul Sloane directed The Woman Accused in 1933, and the film featured Cary Grant.\n- Jacques Demy is best known for the mid-1960s musicals The Umbrellas of Cherbourg (1964) and The Young Girls of Rochefort (1967), which he directed.\n- Paul Sloane directed The Texans, which featured Joan Bennett, Randolph Scott, and Walter Brennan.",
